1
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:12,250
(Seo Hyun Jin)

2
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:15,080
(Yoo Jae Myung)

3
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:18,120
(Lee Si Woo)

4
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,130
(Yoon Se A)

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,340
(Chang Ryul)

6
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,350
(Dahyun)

7
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:54,020
(Love Me)

8
00:00:57,090 --> 00:01:02,400
(Love me)

9
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:07,970
(Love me)

10
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:21,920
By the way,

11
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,550
how come your boyfriend didn't make it today?

12
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,090
Sorry?

13
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,560
I was hoping to finally meet him.

14
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,960
What did you say he does for a living?

15
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,330
She said he'll be a professor soon.

16
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:38,799
No, he's a lecturer, not a professor.

17
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:39,800
I see.

18
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,510
He'll get there eventually. Goodness.

19
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:47,140
A star writer and a professor. What a power couple.

20
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:50,010
See? Now I'm even more curious.

21
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,880
You should've told him to come.

22
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:53,980
I guess he's a little busy.

23
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:58,650
What? Come on. His girlfriend won a major award,

24
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:00,160
and he's "too busy"?

25
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:04,330
Come on, let's go.

26
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:06,630
All right, thanks.

27
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:10,200
You guys go on ahead. I'll be right in.

28
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:12,470
Why? Are you going to call your boyfriend?

29
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:14,670
Tell him to come, even if it's late. I really want to meet him.

30
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:18,210
Hey.

31
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:20,110
Hey!

32
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:30,090
Is this why you didn't show up?

33
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,320
- You can see for yourself. - Why are you working as a driver?

34
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:34,860
I need the money. Am I doing this for fun?

35
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:38,030
That's what I'm asking! What could you need the money for?

36
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:41,499
- I'm busy. I got a ride request. - Seo Jun Seo.

37
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:42,730
For a nobody to become a lecturer,

38
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,170
they said I have to pay 5,000 dollars.

39
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:49,200
They said it's the only way. What else can I do?

40
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,840
You can't be serious.

41
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,280
You'd really pay a bribe for that job?

42
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,050
You'll be a famous author. Can't I have ambitions too?

43
00:02:59,510 --> 00:03:02,080
I have to at least become a lecturer to be a boyfriend you're proud of.

44
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:08,920
- Then you should have told me. - And how was I supposed to do that?

45
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,390
You would've been ashamed.

46
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,390
You can only brag about a professor boyfriend.

47
00:03:13,090 --> 00:03:14,430
Because you're embarrassed I'm a driver,

48
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,300
you lied to them too, didn't you?

49
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:20,800
While I'm losing sleep...

50
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:22,969
driving drunk jerks around,

51
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:24,910
while you're having interviews and going to award shows.

52
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:26,980
And what? Designer clothes?

53
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,380
You think I'll be grateful for thousand-dollar clothes?

54
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,550
Why did you even ask me to come today?

55
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,820
Did you need a pathetic accessory to wear that outfit and applaud you?

56
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,720
- You jerk. - You want me to be more honest?

57
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:43,830
I have absolutely no desire to congratulate you on your award.

58
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:46,600
When you got congratulatory calls, I felt like trash.

59
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:50,600
I felt like a freeloading parasite, and it made me sick to my stomach!

60
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:00,440
So?

61
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:05,750
So, what?

62
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,520
You're trying to get me to break up, aren't you?

63
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,890
You say it. Say you want to break up.

64
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:19,860
Well?

65
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:21,730
You can't even say the words?

66
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,600
Darn.

67
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:33,110
You pathetic fool.

68
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:20,560
Get up. Let's go.

69
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:40,410
You know something?

70
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,580
Jun Kyung lies all the time.

71
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,720
Deep down, she's really weak,

72
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:51,420
but she pretends to be strong, pretends she's okay.

73
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:53,820
She pretends to have it all together,

74
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:56,520
always acting like nothing bothers her.

75
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:01,530
And she's a terrible liar too.

76
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,300
Before,

77
00:06:09,270 --> 00:06:11,140
whenever something was wrong with Jun Kyung,

78
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:15,880
she'd tell me every little detail.

79
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:20,820
But since she met you, having her do that...

80
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:23,720
gotten really rare.

81
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:29,120
I'll admit I'm a little bummed about it.

82
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,730
I kind of hold it against you, actually.

83
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:33,030
But...

84
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,700
I guess that's to be expected.

85
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:38,570
That's why...

86
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,440
when I got her call today,

87
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:43,810
I was like, "Yes!"

88
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,880
I was so excited.

89
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:53,310
But she won't tell me what's wrong.

90
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:57,190
So I didn't push it.

91
00:06:58,050 --> 00:06:59,090
But...

92
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,790
The Jun Kyung I used to know wasn't like this.

93
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:08,360
She'd get angry when she was angry,

94
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,530
and she'd cry when she needed to.

95
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:14,600
Do you...

96
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,840
know what I mean?

97
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:21,640
I do.

98
00:07:24,410 --> 00:07:25,880
Don't make me laugh.

99
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:27,850
You have no idea.

100
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,920
She just kept saying it was all her fault.

101
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,590
Okay, fine.

102
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:38,030
I'm sure Jun Kyung did something wrong.

103
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:40,360
But even so,

104
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:44,070
I'm always on her side, no matter what.

105
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:48,400
I'm completely biased.

106
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:51,770
Thank you.

107
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,450
From now on,

108
00:07:58,910 --> 00:08:01,420
please always be on her side.

109
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,510
I'm holding you to that.

110
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:33,980
- Where's Jun Kyung? - She passed out.

111
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:35,920
My gosh.

112
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,720
Thanks for bringing Soo Jin home, Do Hyun.

113
00:08:40,890 --> 00:08:41,920
And for Jun Kyung too.

114
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:44,790
Get home safe.

115
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:47,730
Let's go.

116
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:32,510
I'm sorry.

117
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:11,110
Hey. What are you doing? Eat up.

118
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:13,980
Your noodles are getting soggy.

119
00:10:14,950 --> 00:10:15,950
Right.

120
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,210
(Management Office)

121
00:10:51,390 --> 00:10:52,390
Ja Yeong.

122
00:10:57,690 --> 00:10:58,690
Ja Yeong.

123
00:11:13,010 --> 00:11:14,180
She...

124
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:16,780
My wife has Alzheimer's disease.

125
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:19,110
Her phone's off. The battery must be dead.

126
00:11:19,150 --> 00:11:21,250
I've searched everywhere around our campsite.

127
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:24,020
We don't have any neighbours, so there's nowhere for her to go.

128
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:27,160
We're reviewing the security video. Just give us a moment.

129
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:31,260
- Okay. - This is the only road out of camp.

130
00:11:33,030 --> 00:11:34,400
She could've gone toward the mountain.

131
00:11:36,930 --> 00:11:40,100
- Has this ever happened before? - No, this is the first time.

132
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:44,110
- Is this you right here, sir? - Yes, that's me.

133
00:11:46,570 --> 00:11:47,810
Could this be her?

134
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,609
It looks like she's looking at you, sir.

135
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:53,150
She seems to be looking at you while on the phone.

136
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:54,920
(Palbon Village Intersection)

137
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:57,090
You didn't run into her then?

138
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:12,470
(Palbon Village Intersection)

139
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:18,140
(Palbon Police Substation)

140
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,590
A work dinner?

141
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,330
You didn't mention that.

142
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:40,730
Yes, it was a last-minute thing.

143
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:43,730
It's one I can't get out of.

144
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:45,800
So I'm probably going to be pretty late.

145
00:12:46,470 --> 00:12:47,500
All right.

146
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:52,010
It's been a while. Have some drinks and enjoy yourself.

147
00:12:52,170 --> 00:12:55,740
Okay, don't wait up. Go on to bed.

148
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:02,580
(Bus Stop)

149
00:13:27,810 --> 00:13:28,910
Hey, Ja Yeong.

150
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,550
Jin Ho.

151
00:13:31,110 --> 00:13:32,280
Did you get on the bus?

152
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,880
No, not yet.

153
00:13:41,290 --> 00:13:42,320
Jin Ho.

154
00:13:44,230 --> 00:13:45,790
So where are you right now?

155
00:13:46,830 --> 00:13:49,200
Listen, Ja Yeong, they're calling for me.

156
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,470
I'll take a cab home, so don't wait up for me.

157
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:54,040
I've got to go.

158
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,040
Jin Ho...

159
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,040
I'm sorry.

160
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,750
I've made things hard on you again.

161
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,790
I truly wanted you to be happy.

162
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:22,990
I thought I could be happy by your side too.

163
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:28,000
But I guess that's not going to happen.

164
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:32,670
Jin Ho.

165
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:35,970
Jin Ho.

166
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:39,640
Jin Ho.

167
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:46,710
I don't know how long I'll have my memories,

168
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:51,650
but I hope my last memory...

169
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,120
is of you.

170
00:17:17,810 --> 00:17:18,840
Are you okay?

171
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:25,510
I'm the one who was wrong. Why are you asking if I'm okay?

172
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,420
You didn't do anything wrong.

173
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:42,500
I'm the one...

174
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:44,630
who's sorry.

175
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:23,500
Thank you for not letting me go.

176
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,190
- Sir. - Yes?

177
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:51,590
You should go home for now.

178
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:54,360
We've been in touch with the taxi company,

179
00:19:54,430 --> 00:19:56,700
so we'll call you the moment we hear from the driver.

180
00:19:58,130 --> 00:19:59,570
No, it's okay. I'll wait.

181
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:02,500
But you've been waiting for so long.

182
00:20:07,010 --> 00:20:09,980
(Serving the community with integrity and care)

183
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:14,680
As you may already know,

184
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,320
a nursing home is different from a convalescent hospital.

185
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:20,620
We focus on providing daily care, not medical treatment.

186
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:23,760
We make sure our residents can eat their meals comfortably...

187
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:26,130
and live in a safe environment.

188
00:20:26,390 --> 00:20:28,330
We provide care for all aspects of their daily lives.

189
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:30,100
It's the easiest way to understand what we do.

190
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:36,600
We have art classes, singing lessons,

191
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:40,010
as well as exercise and a variety of other programs.

192
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:43,110
Our staff members and professional caregivers...

193
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:46,950
treat them like their own family, so you don't need to worry.

194
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:52,190
So, will it be your father or your mother joining us?

195
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,420
It's me.

196
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,210
- Daniel. - I'm not your son?

197
00:21:19,050 --> 00:21:20,050
Am I really...

198
00:21:23,450 --> 00:21:24,790
not your son?

199
00:21:32,090 --> 00:21:33,690
Why did you lie to me?

200
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,530
Daniel, look at me.

201
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:38,630
I wasn't trying to lie to you...

202
00:21:44,910 --> 00:21:46,910
I can't trust anyone anymore.

203
00:21:49,910 --> 00:21:50,940
Mom...

204
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,710
is taking me...

205
00:21:55,250 --> 00:21:56,380
back to Germany.

206
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,620
It's all over now.

207
00:22:04,430 --> 00:22:05,530
Nothing matters anymore.

208
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:21,740
You knew too, didn't you?

209
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:24,810
That day...

210
00:22:27,350 --> 00:22:29,050
when I came to see you...

211
00:22:33,650 --> 00:22:35,020
You knew even then, didn't you?

212
00:22:39,090 --> 00:22:42,700
You know how much I like you.

213
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:45,700
So why? Why didn't you tell me?

214
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:50,000
I didn't have the courage.

215
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:57,340
I was afraid you'd get hurt. I'm so sorry, Daniel.

216
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,580
Because you accepted me...

217
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:08,290
and let me live with you,

218
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,090
I was so...

219
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,500
I was...

220
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:19,030
I was just so happy.

221
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:22,440
I know. I was happy too, son.

222
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,210
I really was so happy.

223
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:39,150
None of that matters to me.

224
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:40,750
I'm...

225
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,290
still your dad,

226
00:23:45,930 --> 00:23:46,960
and you're my son.

227
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,800
Got it?

228
00:24:08,050 --> 00:24:10,080
Yes, this is Officer Park Dong Su from the Palbon Substation.

229
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,120
Yes.

230
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:17,160
Yes, you said you've located him?

231
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,160
Yes.

232
00:24:28,970 --> 00:24:29,970
Yes, I see.

233
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:38,380
This stop is the Ian City Promotion Hall.

234
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:41,850
Next stop, Power Square Mall.

235
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:46,920
("A Still Relationship")

236
00:24:56,960 --> 00:25:00,370
(The hit new novel, "A Still Relationship" by Ji Hye On)

237
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:11,210
("A Still Relationship")

238
00:25:11,810 --> 00:25:13,450
(Ji Hye On)

239
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:33,700
(Professor Song Won Cheol)

240
00:25:38,340 --> 00:25:39,370
Tonight,

241
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:43,980
with the guy who's always been there for me,

242
00:25:45,310 --> 00:25:47,410
instead of some fancy steak and whiskey,

243
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:51,990
I want to celebrate with a beer and a pork cutlet from our local joint.

244
00:25:54,290 --> 00:25:55,590
And tomorrow night...

245
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:58,760
and the night after that...

246
00:25:58,830 --> 00:26:00,960
(On the 29th night of summer, Ji Hye On)

247
00:26:01,030 --> 00:26:05,000
I want to tell him I just want us to stay like this forever.

248
00:26:06,830 --> 00:26:12,270
("A Still Relationship")

249
00:26:27,790 --> 00:26:28,990
Aren't you going to answer that?

250
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:32,390
Your mom must be worried.

251
00:26:34,290 --> 00:26:35,300
I don't want to.

252
00:26:49,410 --> 00:26:50,440
Let's eat first.

253
00:26:51,750 --> 00:26:53,550
You must be starving. You haven't eaten anything.

254
00:26:54,980 --> 00:26:57,620
Eat up, and then I'll take you home.

255
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:17,100
(Police)

256
00:27:19,540 --> 00:27:20,570
Are you Daniel?

257
00:27:25,010 --> 00:27:27,010
- Yes. - Your mother reported you missing.

258
00:27:28,020 --> 00:27:31,080
She said you weren't taking calls and thought you were here.

259
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:33,520
Come out, Daniel.

260
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:36,990
What do you think you're doing?

261
00:27:37,590 --> 00:27:40,260
What's it to you? What are you, Daniel's dad?

262
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,060
What do you think you're doing?

263
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,870
Please bring my son out here.

264
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:50,870
Is this woman your mother?

265
00:27:56,410 --> 00:27:58,710
And is he your father?

266
00:28:09,490 --> 00:28:12,160
For now, I think it's best if you go with your mom.

267
00:28:28,980 --> 00:28:30,980
- Daniel. - Sir.

268
00:28:32,380 --> 00:28:33,550
This is the last time.

269
00:28:34,010 --> 00:28:36,280
You will never see Daniel again.

270
00:28:55,740 --> 00:28:56,740
Daniel.

271
00:29:04,410 --> 00:29:06,110
Don't cry. You're not a little kid anymore.

272
00:29:08,250 --> 00:29:09,450
What are you doing?

273
00:29:12,090 --> 00:29:13,590
No matter what anyone else says,

274
00:29:13,820 --> 00:29:15,660
what you want is most important. You know that, right?

275
00:29:17,260 --> 00:29:19,490
Do what your heart tells you. Whatever that is.

276
00:29:23,660 --> 00:29:24,660
Get in.

277
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:36,010
You said you'd do anything for him. Is this what's best for him?

278
00:29:37,010 --> 00:29:39,210
I don't think that's any of your business.

279
00:29:55,860 --> 00:29:57,460
Oh, her?

280
00:29:58,230 --> 00:30:00,330
She had a consultation and left a little while ago.

281
00:30:25,860 --> 00:30:29,730
There's something magical about sunset.

282
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:31,200
(For rent)

283
00:30:33,030 --> 00:30:35,670
New buildings and old ones,

284
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:41,580
people laughing and people fighting...

285
00:30:44,580 --> 00:30:47,910
At this hour, everything just looks equally beautiful, you know?

286
00:30:54,150 --> 00:30:55,290
I used to...

287
00:30:56,990 --> 00:30:59,690
feel so at peace watching the sunset.

288
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:03,560
I'd think, "Another day well-lived."

289
00:31:05,930 --> 00:31:06,930
But these days,

290
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:10,140
it just makes me sad.

291
00:31:13,740 --> 00:31:15,540
It's like, "There goes another day."

292
00:31:20,650 --> 00:31:23,650
I used to feel that way too.

293
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:48,140
Are you really not going back to him?

294
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:52,250
Why?

295
00:31:53,450 --> 00:31:54,610
Because you think without him,

296
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:57,520
I won't be okay?

297
00:31:58,490 --> 00:31:59,490
No.

298
00:32:00,750 --> 00:32:02,120
Without you,

299
00:32:02,660 --> 00:32:04,260
I don't think he'll be okay.

300
00:32:08,860 --> 00:32:12,000
You know what a mess he is.

301
00:32:14,370 --> 00:32:15,470
Sometimes...

302
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:19,210
I even miss his awful jokes.

303
00:32:21,470 --> 00:32:22,480
You're right.

304
00:32:23,610 --> 00:32:25,080
They're really not funny.

305
00:32:33,220 --> 00:32:34,220
He...

306
00:32:35,290 --> 00:32:38,330
is probably still waiting for you.

307
00:33:28,780 --> 00:33:30,480
Look at the state of you.

308
00:33:33,910 --> 00:33:34,950
I thought you said I looked fine.

309
00:33:37,450 --> 00:33:39,250
You really are a mess without me.

310
00:33:41,890 --> 00:33:43,020
I know.

311
00:33:45,790 --> 00:33:46,960
Without you,

312
00:33:48,530 --> 00:33:49,530
I'm a mess.

313
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:53,500
So...

314
00:34:01,710 --> 00:34:02,710
So, please...

315
00:34:04,580 --> 00:34:05,610
don't leave me.

316
00:34:24,730 --> 00:34:27,670
You win everything you touch. Good heavens.

317
00:34:32,310 --> 00:34:34,670
What's with the surprise visit? You didn't even call.

318
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:36,940
I want my money back.

319
00:34:38,650 --> 00:34:39,650
What?

320
00:34:40,710 --> 00:34:41,880
I'm turning down the lecturer job.

321
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:44,550
Hey, what's gotten into you?

322
00:34:44,620 --> 00:34:46,290
I'm not interested in buying a teaching position.

323
00:34:46,720 --> 00:34:48,960
And besides, I never wanted to be a lecturer.

324
00:34:51,090 --> 00:34:52,090
Give me my money back.

325
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:55,700
Hey, what do you think you're... No, I...

326
00:35:00,100 --> 00:35:04,570
Nationality, gender, age, social status, language...

327
00:35:05,340 --> 00:35:06,970
Two people who seemed to have nothing in common.

328
00:35:09,580 --> 00:35:11,880
For Emma and Ryan, in the unfamiliar land of Korea,

329
00:35:12,180 --> 00:35:14,480
the only way they could communicate...

330
00:35:15,050 --> 00:35:16,680
was through their broken Korean.

331
00:35:19,090 --> 00:35:22,190
But the two do share one other thing.

332
00:35:25,460 --> 00:35:26,460
Loneliness.

333
00:35:29,930 --> 00:35:32,030
Which brings me to a question.

334
00:35:32,670 --> 00:35:36,400
Do you have a favourite line from the book?

335
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:41,110
- Sorry? - I'm sure you love all you wrote,

336
00:35:41,570 --> 00:35:46,080
but our Night Walk family is curious to know your absolute favourite.

337
00:35:57,490 --> 00:36:00,660
Noticing the shadow on Emma's face, Ryan asked,

338
00:36:02,130 --> 00:36:03,130
"What's wrong?"

339
00:36:06,670 --> 00:36:08,300
"The milk bottles in front of my neighbour's door..."

340
00:36:08,770 --> 00:36:12,370
"kept piling up, so I rang his bell."

341
00:36:13,940 --> 00:36:15,640
"But no one answered."

342
00:36:18,710 --> 00:36:19,710
"It was a lonely death."

343
00:36:23,150 --> 00:36:24,150
"A lonely death?"

344
00:36:25,650 --> 00:36:26,650
"Yes."

345
00:36:27,890 --> 00:36:29,190
"He died from loneliness."

346
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:34,390
"Then, after a long silence, Emma spoke."

347
00:36:36,460 --> 00:36:37,630
"Isn't that terrifying?"

348
00:36:38,970 --> 00:36:39,970
"The thought that loneliness..."

349
00:36:41,100 --> 00:36:43,240
"can actually be a cause of death."

350
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:51,140
"Ryan held Emma in his arms."

351
00:36:55,620 --> 00:36:56,850
"And he told her,"

352
00:37:00,090 --> 00:37:01,450
- "It's why some people..." - "It's why some people..."

353
00:37:04,890 --> 00:37:06,060
"need someone else."

354
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:13,170
"The way I need you."

355
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:20,540
So you finally read it?

356
00:37:25,850 --> 00:37:28,580
It was really well written.

357
00:37:31,650 --> 00:37:32,750
You deserved the award.

358
00:37:35,990 --> 00:37:38,930
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

359
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:44,160
Congratulations.

360
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:50,770
And I guess you're not going to apologise?

361
00:37:53,410 --> 00:37:55,440
I'm sorry. I really am.

362
00:38:05,420 --> 00:38:06,620
Not your hand.

363
00:38:08,490 --> 00:38:09,720
Give me my book.

364
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:14,460
- What? - I said, give it back.

365
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:17,260
Right.

366
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,980
I didn't sign one for anyone else. I saved the first for you.

367
00:38:33,150 --> 00:38:35,880
("A Still Relationship")

368
00:38:36,580 --> 00:38:37,620
My very first autograph.

369
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:39,620
(To my Squirtle, Seo Jun Seo, From Ji Hye On)

370
00:38:39,690 --> 00:38:41,390
I got a lot of criticisms for it.

371
00:38:42,090 --> 00:38:43,620
They said a rookie was putting on airs.

372
00:38:55,100 --> 00:38:56,100
Why?

373
00:38:58,840 --> 00:38:59,870
You know...

374
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:03,810
You really look like Emma Stone.

375
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:10,820
Says Ryan Gosling.

376
00:39:26,670 --> 00:39:27,670
I'm hungry.

377
00:39:28,630 --> 00:39:29,700
Let's go get some pork cutlets.

378
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Should we?

379
00:39:33,410 --> 00:39:35,610
It's on me. I'm loaded.

380
00:39:36,510 --> 00:39:37,810
Since when do you have money?

381
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:40,610
I got the 5,000 dollars back.

382
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:42,180
I'm not taking the job.

383
00:39:42,650 --> 00:39:43,650
Really?

384
00:39:44,380 --> 00:39:45,380
Then what are you going to do?

385
00:39:45,890 --> 00:39:47,420
I'll have to figure it out. Starting now.

386
00:39:48,690 --> 00:39:49,690
Good for you.

387
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:52,490
Being an instructor didn't suit you anyway.

388
00:39:53,430 --> 00:39:56,760
But I can still afford to buy you beer and pork cutlets anytime.

389
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:06,610
(Gestational Age: 20 weeks, Fetal Ultrasound Photo)

390
00:40:07,810 --> 00:40:11,880
(Next Appointment: In 2 weeks)

391
00:40:16,120 --> 00:40:19,450
(The day you were born)

392
00:40:43,710 --> 00:40:45,010
Please take good care of Oscar.

393
00:40:46,950 --> 00:40:47,950
I will.

394
00:40:49,450 --> 00:40:50,480
Take care of yourself.

395
00:40:54,390 --> 00:40:55,920
I'll call you sometimes.

396
00:41:07,870 --> 00:41:08,900
Mom.

397
00:41:10,040 --> 00:41:11,500
Can I go talk to him for a minute?

398
00:41:12,740 --> 00:41:14,010
Don't be too long.

399
00:41:16,110 --> 00:41:17,110
Okay.

400
00:41:46,540 --> 00:41:47,910
Is your hand all right now?

401
00:41:52,610 --> 00:41:54,050
A scar from my defeat, I suppose.

402
00:41:57,680 --> 00:42:00,090
Congratulations. You won.

403
00:42:02,860 --> 00:42:04,660
You must think this is some kind of game.

404
00:42:08,530 --> 00:42:12,229
Strangely, it doesn't feel awkward being alone with you like this.

405
00:42:12,230 --> 00:42:13,600
Why did it have to be Do Hyun?

406
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:21,140
You came all this way just to ask me that?

407
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:34,390
(Maternal Health Handbook)

408
00:42:34,450 --> 00:42:35,920
And I had something to return to you.

409
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:42,660
It's a common story.

410
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:45,870
A one-night mistake.

411
00:42:48,970 --> 00:42:51,970
After Do Hyun and I broke up, I was struggling and so lonely.

412
00:42:54,470 --> 00:42:56,240
And I was only 20 back then.

413
00:42:57,710 --> 00:43:01,080
I ended up pregnant and was terrified,

414
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:06,590
but sweet Do Hyun fell for my lie and was overjoyed.

415
00:43:09,060 --> 00:43:11,420
That's why I decided to have Daniel.

416
00:43:14,290 --> 00:43:15,830
I guess that must be why...

417
00:43:16,730 --> 00:43:20,430
I tricked myself into thinking Do Hyun could fill this emptiness.

418
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:23,570
But you know, Yoon Ju...

419
00:43:26,310 --> 00:43:29,940
loneliness doesn't give you a free pass.

420
00:44:04,780 --> 00:44:05,780
All this time,

421
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:12,790
it's been great.

422
00:44:16,590 --> 00:44:17,590
Thanks to you.

423
00:44:24,530 --> 00:44:25,770
I didn't know you could talk like that.

424
00:44:34,540 --> 00:44:35,540
So now,

425
00:44:38,310 --> 00:44:39,880
are you not going to call me Dad anymore?

426
00:44:59,170 --> 00:45:00,400
I should get going now.

427
00:45:12,310 --> 00:45:14,010
Be happy with Jun Kyung.

428
00:45:18,980 --> 00:45:19,990
Okay.

429
00:45:26,590 --> 00:45:28,390
I think I'm going to miss you a lot.

430
00:45:33,700 --> 00:45:34,700
Dad.

431
00:46:19,810 --> 00:46:21,710
I wish I could've treated you to somewhere nicer.

432
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:24,220
What could possibly be better than this?

433
00:46:27,020 --> 00:46:29,120
I'm so glad you seem to be okay.

434
00:46:30,720 --> 00:46:32,020
I was really worried about you.

435
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:38,430
When most people find out about a thing like that,

436
00:46:40,230 --> 00:46:44,600
they're too embarrassed to reach out.

437
00:46:45,440 --> 00:46:48,470
I'm sorry. Did I overstep?

438
00:46:49,410 --> 00:46:50,410
No.

439
00:46:51,440 --> 00:46:52,610
I'm trying to thank you.

440
00:46:54,250 --> 00:46:55,710
For checking in on me and worrying.

441
00:46:58,780 --> 00:46:59,890
But...

442
00:47:01,050 --> 00:47:03,390
I have a concern of my own. May I ask you something?

443
00:47:04,390 --> 00:47:06,429
- Sure. - Aren't you seeing anyone?

444
00:47:06,430 --> 00:47:07,430
Like a boyfriend?

445
00:47:09,360 --> 00:47:12,630
Spending a perfect day off like this with me, of all people.

446
00:47:16,070 --> 00:47:17,340
There was...

447
00:47:18,770 --> 00:47:20,070
someone I liked.

448
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:24,980
"Was"? So you two broke up?

449
00:47:26,450 --> 00:47:27,450
No.

450
00:47:29,950 --> 00:47:31,980
He doesn't even know that I liked him.

451
00:47:33,250 --> 00:47:35,020
It was just a one-sided crush,

452
00:47:35,650 --> 00:47:37,620
and in the meantime, he got a girlfriend.

453
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:40,990
What? If you started to like him,

454
00:47:41,590 --> 00:47:43,160
you should have told him.

455
00:47:45,970 --> 00:47:48,100
It's easy to like someone from afar,

456
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:55,470
but I guess dating and getting to know someone scared me.

457
00:47:58,080 --> 00:47:59,510
I'm not very courageous, you know.

458
00:48:03,220 --> 00:48:04,620
That's true.

459
00:48:05,850 --> 00:48:10,490
There's misunderstanding, jealousy, fighting, and making up.

460
00:48:12,460 --> 00:48:15,330
All those emotions you can afford to be lazy with when you're alone...

461
00:48:15,490 --> 00:48:17,930
suddenly have to work overtime.

462
00:48:19,370 --> 00:48:20,370
Gosh...

463
00:48:22,570 --> 00:48:25,540
You may not have found the courage to say anything yet,

464
00:48:25,640 --> 00:48:27,970
but I bet someone out there has a crush on you.

465
00:48:31,010 --> 00:48:32,010
Come on.

466
00:48:34,410 --> 00:48:35,780
Should we try being brave together?

467
00:48:42,390 --> 00:48:45,490
But is this really considered being brave?

468
00:48:46,590 --> 00:48:49,930
Isn't trying something new an act of courage?

469
00:48:54,630 --> 00:48:58,170
- Have you ever had a wavy perm? - No, this is my first time.

470
00:48:59,370 --> 00:49:00,840
I think it'll look great on you.

471
00:49:01,610 --> 00:49:04,010
- Then let's get started. - Okay.

472
00:49:33,810 --> 00:49:34,810
Gosh.

473
00:49:35,140 --> 00:49:37,910
What? Does it look weird?

474
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:41,410
It's because you're so beautiful.

475
00:49:42,720 --> 00:49:44,380
You keep taking my breath away.

476
00:49:58,760 --> 00:50:00,100
This looks about right, doesn't it?

477
00:50:00,530 --> 00:50:02,770
Yes, Hye On, you're a natural.

478
00:50:02,840 --> 00:50:06,310
- The best learn from the best. - And you've got the banter down.

479
00:50:06,410 --> 00:50:08,240
- I'm just going to grab a rag. - Yes, go ahead.

480
00:50:09,440 --> 00:50:11,910
Gosh, you can tell you've done this before.

481
00:50:12,410 --> 00:50:14,180
How's the job hunt going?

482
00:50:14,650 --> 00:50:15,810
Yes, it's going fine.

483
00:50:16,120 --> 00:50:17,520
I'm sure it is.

484
00:50:17,950 --> 00:50:20,850
Undergrad astronomy, your master's in "interdisciplinary studies,"

485
00:50:20,920 --> 00:50:23,020
and now you're applying to the National Weather Service?

486
00:50:23,860 --> 00:50:26,490
You want to forecast the weather when you can't fix your own life?

487
00:50:26,560 --> 00:50:28,660
I'm trying to get my life together, you know?

488
00:50:28,730 --> 00:50:31,430
For the record, it's been a while since I asked you for money.

489
00:50:31,500 --> 00:50:32,560
So stop nagging me.

490
00:50:32,660 --> 00:50:34,670
You still haven't fully paid me back, you know.

491
00:50:36,940 --> 00:50:39,570
Do we have to do this at home? We could just go out instead.

492
00:50:39,640 --> 00:50:41,810
Why are you suddenly doing something so out of character?

493
00:50:41,870 --> 00:50:45,440
If we go out, are you paying? If we stay home, are you cooking?

494
00:50:45,580 --> 00:50:49,350
- Kids! The kimchi is here! - You're here, Uncle!

495
00:50:49,580 --> 00:50:51,550
Hey, take this. I have to use the restroom.

496
00:50:51,620 --> 00:50:54,450
Gosh, this guy. He was like this the whole way here.

497
00:50:54,520 --> 00:50:58,960
- Auntie, I'll put this away. - Okay. Something smells delicious!

498
00:50:59,020 --> 00:51:00,160
- You're here. - Hello.

499
00:51:00,230 --> 00:51:01,230
- Hi. - Hello.

500
00:51:01,630 --> 00:51:03,160
- We're here! - Come on in.

501
00:51:03,230 --> 00:51:04,230
Hello, everyone.

502
00:51:04,830 --> 00:51:06,330
- Dad, you're here? - Yes.

503
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:08,030
- You're here, Dad. - You made it, Ja Yeong.

504
00:51:08,100 --> 00:51:10,200
- Welcome. - Oh, my, Jun Kyung, your hair...

505
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:12,240
Why? Does it look weird?

506
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:15,710
- You look beautiful! It's great! - Really?

507
00:51:15,770 --> 00:51:17,940
- You made it. - Yes, I'm here.

508
00:51:18,140 --> 00:51:21,250
- Hello, Ja Yeong. - Hello, Uncle.

509
00:51:21,350 --> 00:51:24,950
Jun Kyung, what's with your hair? I liked it much better before.

510
00:51:25,020 --> 00:51:28,020
- This guy. - But she just said it was pretty...

511
00:51:28,350 --> 00:51:29,720
Sorry.

512
00:51:30,020 --> 00:51:31,820
Since when have we had a dining table this big?

513
00:51:32,090 --> 00:51:35,260
I just bought it. I figured it'd be useful someday.

514
00:51:35,390 --> 00:51:37,600
- Good call. - Dad, the picture frame too.

515
00:51:38,060 --> 00:51:39,260
Goodness.

516
00:51:40,970 --> 00:51:41,970
Gosh.

517
00:51:42,900 --> 00:51:43,900
What do you think?

518
00:51:44,340 --> 00:51:46,040
Gosh.

519
00:51:48,210 --> 00:51:49,210
Goodness.

520
00:52:15,200 --> 00:52:17,840
- Happy birthday to you - Happy birthday to you

521
00:52:18,100 --> 00:52:20,910
- Happy birthday to you - Happy birthday to you

522
00:52:21,110 --> 00:52:24,410
- Happy birthday, dear Ja Yeong - Happy birthday, dear Ja Yeong

523
00:52:24,710 --> 00:52:27,849
- Happy birthday to you - Happy birthday to you

524
00:52:27,850 --> 00:52:28,980
Hold on.

525
00:52:30,350 --> 00:52:33,850
I have something to say before I blow out the candles.

526
00:52:35,950 --> 00:52:37,560
Judging by your smile, it must be something good.

527
00:52:38,390 --> 00:52:40,360
Did you win the lottery?

528
00:52:40,760 --> 00:52:43,330
- Sadly, no. - Dad, are you two getting married?

529
00:52:43,660 --> 00:52:45,830
- Oh, my. - Married? Don't be ridiculous.

530
00:52:48,370 --> 00:52:51,100
Well, I...

531
00:52:52,570 --> 00:52:55,010
I have Alzheimer's.

532
00:53:13,330 --> 00:53:15,230
It's progressing quickly,

533
00:53:15,790 --> 00:53:17,660
and the prognosis isn't good.

534
00:53:18,730 --> 00:53:23,370
So I've been getting treatment and learning how to manage it,

535
00:53:24,500 --> 00:53:28,010
and Jin Ho, in case I get lost,

536
00:53:28,770 --> 00:53:32,910
has put up signs all over the camp ground for me.

537
00:53:34,250 --> 00:53:36,850
I have to learn to live with my disease now.

538
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:41,150
I don't know when, but eventually,

539
00:53:44,690 --> 00:53:47,160
I'll stop recognising all of you too.

540
00:53:55,400 --> 00:53:58,440
If I don't recognise you and hurt you,

541
00:53:59,040 --> 00:54:01,210
please don't hate me for it.

542
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:07,280
I wanted to apologise in advance and ask you for this favour.

543
00:54:24,300 --> 00:54:25,930
Thank you, Jun Kyung,

544
00:54:26,900 --> 00:54:29,070
for throwing me such a lovely birthday party.

545
00:54:36,380 --> 00:54:40,410
Don't worry, Auntie. I think you'll be the last I forget.

546
00:54:40,810 --> 00:54:43,150
That charisma you had when we first met...

547
00:54:43,420 --> 00:54:45,150
How could I ever forget that?

548
00:54:48,820 --> 00:54:52,990
I'm going to make a wish and blow out my candles now.

549
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:05,960
("A Still Relationship")

550
00:56:26,220 --> 00:56:27,320
You doing okay?

551
00:56:27,890 --> 00:56:30,420
What now? Did you call to pick a fight?

552
00:56:30,920 --> 00:56:32,990
No, I called to say congratulations.

553
00:56:34,490 --> 00:56:36,430
You're a real meteorologist now.

554
00:56:36,660 --> 00:56:39,200
But can I even trust your forecasts?

555
00:56:39,770 --> 00:56:40,770
Suit yourself.

556
00:56:41,230 --> 00:56:42,730
Now hurry up and pay me back.

557
00:56:43,030 --> 00:56:45,540
The second I get my paycheck, I'll pay you back first thing.

558
00:56:45,800 --> 00:56:46,940
Please do.

559
00:56:47,270 --> 00:56:48,440
I'm busy. I have to go.

560
00:56:52,280 --> 00:56:53,910
- Jun Kyung. - What?

561
00:56:55,550 --> 00:56:56,750
It's supposed to rain tomorrow.

562
00:56:57,580 --> 00:56:58,620
Bring an umbrella.

563
00:57:00,190 --> 00:57:01,190
All right.

564
00:57:19,840 --> 00:57:22,010
Dad, are you doing okay?

565
00:57:22,770 --> 00:57:27,310
I'm great. The hospital treatment you suggested is going very well.

566
00:57:27,850 --> 00:57:30,480
These days, Ja Yeong is even better at finding her way around than I am.

567
00:57:32,750 --> 00:57:35,550
How have you been? Are the wedding plans coming along?

568
00:57:36,620 --> 00:57:37,620
Yes.

569
00:57:38,220 --> 00:57:41,190
Do Hyun and I went to an adoption agency yesterday.

570
00:57:41,490 --> 00:57:44,160
Really? That's great.

571
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:49,430
Yes. But I'm still not sure about it.

572
00:57:51,670 --> 00:57:53,570
Take your time to think it over.

573
00:57:54,110 --> 00:57:56,880
Whatever you decide, I know you two will do great.

574
00:57:57,480 --> 00:57:58,480
Okay, Dad.

575
00:58:08,450 --> 00:58:09,890
Someone once said...

576
00:58:11,390 --> 00:58:12,960
that happiness is quiet...

577
00:58:14,290 --> 00:58:15,930
and misery is loud.

578
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:19,730
In that sense, maybe happiness...

579
00:58:21,770 --> 00:58:23,740
is a lot like loneliness.

580
00:58:25,770 --> 00:58:27,040
Different in shape,

581
00:58:28,470 --> 00:58:29,740
different in colour,

582
00:58:31,380 --> 00:58:32,540
and different in size.

583
00:58:35,680 --> 00:58:37,550
The loneliness each of us feels.

584
00:58:41,590 --> 00:58:43,420
But if you trace it back to its source,

585
00:58:43,960 --> 00:58:46,960
they say you'll find love at the very end.

586
00:58:49,060 --> 00:58:52,060
When you crave something but can't have it,

587
00:58:53,530 --> 00:58:55,200
when you're left wanting,

588
00:58:58,070 --> 00:59:00,510
that feeling of emptiness is what becomes loneliness.

589
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:07,850
When you look at it that way, maybe being lonely isn't so bad after all.

590
00:59:09,810 --> 00:59:12,020
It just hasn't been fulfilled yet,

591
00:59:13,450 --> 00:59:15,190
but at least it proves...

592
00:59:17,290 --> 00:59:18,760
that just as much love

593
00:59:21,330 --> 00:59:22,390
exists within my heart.

594
00:59:33,340 --> 00:59:35,840
(Love Me)

595
01:00:46,010 --> 01:00:50,480
(Thank you for watching Love Me.)
